  <section id="desktop" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Desktop tree</h2>
    <p>
      Rules are in <code>apps/desktop/src/README.md</code> and <code>specs/06-desktop-ui.md</code>.
      A feature folder contains only the subfolders it uses. Shared code moves to
      <code>src/shared</code> when a second feature needs it. <code>src/pages</code> stays a
      one-line adapter.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="text" title="apps/desktop/src">
{`app/          Shell.tsx, routes.tsx, client.ts, sidecar.ts, PageStub.tsx
pages/        route adapters
features/     admin, ai, analytics, auth, billing, cad, cam, chat,
              companion, costs, dashboard, legal, library, marketplace,
              mcp, organizations, plugins, profile, projects, settings,
              toolpaths
shared/       ui, components, state
styles/       global CSS
viewport/     editor2d, view3d, spatial, units.ts
i18n/         tables, default locale en
testing/      fake API and core-flow tests
main.tsx`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      Inside a feature, the allowed folder names are <code>screens/</code>,
      <code>components/</code>, <code>hooks/</code>, <code>lib/</code>, <code>store/</code>,
      <code>types/</code>, <code>api/</code>, and <code>styles/</code>. CAD currently has
      <code>components</code>, <code>hooks</code>, <code>lib</code>, <code>screens</code>,
      <code>store</code>, and <code>types</code>. Add a folder only when that feature needs it.
    </p>
    <p>
      The webview dev server is Vite at <code>http://localhost:1420</code>
      (<code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/tauri.conf.json</code>). The Rust shell’s identifier is
      <code>com.cadcamfun.app</code>. Sidecar binaries are
      <code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/binaries/sidecar-&lt;host-triple&gt;</code>. Bundled migration
      SQL is <code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/resources/migrations/</code>, copied from
      <code>packages/db/drizzle</code> by <code>bun run build:sidecar</code>. The stub compiler is
      <code>apps/desktop/scripts/build-stub-sidecar.ts</code> and the stub source is
      <code>apps/desktop/src-tauri/stub/stub-sidecar.ts</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCallout title="PageStub.tsx is still in the tree" type="note">
      <p>
        <code>apps/desktop/src/app/PageStub.tsx</code> exists. <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §4
        says the rest of the 65 pages are still stubs. The roadmap snapshot says pages are no
        longer <code>PageStub</code>. Read <code>apps/desktop/src/app/routes.tsx</code> before
        you delete or rename the component. Do not pick a status from this paragraph.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
  </section>

  <section id="sidecar" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Sidecar and API</h2>
    <p>
      HTTP handler files under <code>apps/sidecar/src/http</code> include
      <code>health.ts</code>, <code>projects.ts</code>, <code>drawings.ts</code>,
      <code>toolpaths.ts</code>, <code>toolpath-generator.ts</code>, <code>tools.ts</code>,
      <code>materials.ts</code>, <code>machine-configs.ts</code>, <code>library.ts</code>,
      <code>ai.ts</code>, <code>plugins.ts</code>, <code>auth.ts</code>, <code>vcs.ts</code>,
      <code>companion.ts</code>, <code>billing.ts</code>, <code>organizations.ts</code>,
      <code>files.ts</code>, <code>kv.ts</code>, and <code>waitlist.ts</code> (the directory has
      more; list it before assuming a route is missing). Matching contract groups live in
      <code>packages/api/src/groups</code>. A handler without a group, or a group without a
      handler, is the parity gap <code>specs/11-api-parity-brief.md</code> tracks. WP4’s §4 status
      says every contract group is served and families without a contract are still missing.
    </p>
    <p>
      Service modules under <code>apps/sidecar/src/services</code> include <code>ai.ts</code>,
      <code>cam-program.ts</code>, <code>project-vcs.ts</code>, <code>workflow-runner.ts</code>,
      <code>companion-gateway.ts</code>, <code>payments.ts</code>, <code>kv.ts</code>, and
      <code>local-profile.ts</code>. Repositories under <code>src/repos</code> are the Drizzle
      calls. Other packages do not open SQLite. They call these services or, inside
      <code>packages/db</code> tests, <code>Database.query</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash" title="Contract commands, from the repo root">
{`bun run --filter @cadcamfun/api coverage
bun run generate
bun run generate:check
bunx tsc -p packages/api/tsconfig.json
bunx tsc -p apps/sidecar/tsconfig.json`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      <code>coverage</code> is <code>packages/api/scripts/api-coverage.ts</code>. The task board
      records its result as 67/195. The roadmap snapshot records 121/195. Run the command and read
      the output. <code>generate</code> rewrites <code>packages/api/src/sdk</code> and
      <code>packages/api/src/client</code> from the HttpApi contract via
      <code>@cadcamfun/httpapi-codegen</code>. Commit generated clients only when you were asked
      to commit.
    </p>
  </section>

