        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section id="contracts" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Contracts</h2>
    <p>
      Dependency direction: <code>core</code> ← <code>api</code> ← sidecar;
      <code>db</code> ← sidecar; <code>ai</code> and <code>plugin-sdk</code> ← sidecar. The desktop
      imports API types only, and its <code>package.json</code> also depends on
      <code>@cadcamfun/core</code>. <code>core</code> and <code>api</code> must not import
      <code>db</code>. Only <code>packages/db</code> talks to SQLite. Everyone else uses a sidecar
      repository service or the <code>Database</code> service.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>.reference/</code> is the legacy Next.js and Prisma tree. It is read-only. v6 does not
      import it. Do not read <code>.env*</code> files. Do not hand-edit SQL in
      <code>packages/db/drizzle/</code>. Effect stays at <code>4.0.0-rc.112</code>, with docs in
      <code>packages/db/node_modules/effect/ai-docs/src/</code>.
    </p>
    <DocCode language="bash" title="Open the area you are about to edit">
{`bunx tsc -p packages/core/tsconfig.json
bun test packages/core
bun run desktop:dev`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      <code>desktop:dev</code> builds the sidecar first. The window’s database is
      <code>$CADCAMFUN_DATA_DIR/cadcamfun.db</code> (Tauri <code>app_data_dir</code>), not the CLI
      file <code>bun run db:migrate</code> writes. See <a href="/docs/guides/local-dev">Local development</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
